// x-typecheck-generics-F1: `$` over an open cell: --check accepts, elaboration refuses
//
// command: graphix --check design/review-2026-10-05/repro/x-typecheck-generics-F1.gx
//          graphix --no-cache design/review-2026-10-05/repro/x-typecheck-generics-F1.gx
//          graphix-fuzz check design/review-2026-10-05/repro/x-typecheck-generics-F1.gx
//
// expected: the check and the build agree. `1$` and `|x: i64| x$` are refused
// by the check ("cannot use the $ operator on i64, it has no error and no
// null"), so f(1) should be refused by the check too (or both should accept).
//
// observed: --check exits 0 (f: fn(x: 'a) -> 'a). The run exits 1:
//   in the instance of f(1) at this call site ... in: x$:
//   cannot use the $ operator on i64, it has no error and no null
// graphix-fuzz check: "DIVERGENCE — the check accepted what the build refused"
// and GRAPHIX_ELAB_AUDIT=1 prints an ELAB-AUDIT line at `x$`. Same with
// `|x: 'a| x$` and with `let g = |xs| array::map(xs, |x| x$); g([1, 2])`.
// Called through a function value the check cannot resolve (`let g = select
// b { true => f, false => f }; g(1)`), the run-time bind logs "a run-time bind
// at g(1) did not type" and runs anyway.
let f = |x| x$;
f(1)
